2026-11-15  Second independent content verification (a verifier that wrote none of the package)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Method: all 73 recorded pages fetched afresh. The four primers' chapters and the cited entries
of Ibn al-Mundhir and Ibn Hazm were read in full; every Bidayat al-Mujtahid quote was read with
the sentences around it, and the tayammum chapter's Bab 1, 6 and 7 in full. Each claim, position,
card and check question was read against that Arabic. Entry numbers (Ibn al-Mundhir nos. 2, 11,
12, 14, 15, 18, 19, 21, 25, 31), chapter names and print pages were checked against the page
headings of the online copies: all as recorded.
- tools/verify-citations.mjs: all quotes found before the changes (161) and after (163).
  build-deen.mjs --check: 9 of 9 shipped.
- The unit ships no hadith item, dhikr, dua or grading; nothing here needs a two-witness
  collation or an attributed verdict.
Findings fixed (tayammum-06 raised to rev 3):
1. tayammum-06/c6 Maliki: "a resident who is ill" misread "لضرر بجسمه مقيم". "مقيم" describes
   the harm, not the person: al-Thamar al-Dani on this line glosses it "أي مرض لازم وبقي إلى وقت
   الصلاة الثانية" (shamela.ws/book/7441/75). Now "a sick person who cannot touch water because
   of a lasting harm to his body". "The primer also records other views" is replaced by the
   view the primer gives next, "وقد قيل يتيمم لكل صلاة" (quote extended to include it).
   Position text and school card.
2. tayammum-06/c2: Ibn Hazm's agreement that tayammum stands in for ghusl as well as wudu was
   given without the difference Ibn Rushd records in Bab 1: "واختلفوا في الكبرى فروي عن عمر
   وابن مسعود أنهما كانا لا يريانها بدلا من الكبرى ... وبه قال عامة الفقهاء". The claim now
   notes that early difference and that jurists generally hold it does. Cross-location recorded.
3. tayammum-06/c5: Ibn al-Mundhir's agreement on finding water before the prayer was given
   bare, while Ibn Rushd (Bab 6, mas'ala 2) has it as the majority's view against "وذهب قوم
   إلى أن الناقض لها هو الحدث". The claim now attributes the agreement to Ibn al-Mundhir and
   notes what Ibn Rushd records. Cross-location recorded. The card and check question keep
   the answer Ibn al-Mundhir reports.
Read and left as they are:
- ghusl-05/c3: Ibn Rushd opens the mas'ala with a difference among the Companions on
  intercourse without emission. The claim states only what the four primers list, which is
  accurate for all four; the cross-location stays on record.
- khuff-07/c3: Ibn Rushd gives Malik's view as the top obligatory and the bottom recommended;
  al-Risala only describes wiping both, and the position says no more than that.
- najasa-08/c3: "that died without being slaughtered" glosses "ميتة"; Ibn Rushd's sentence has
  the word alone. Kept as a plain-English rendering of the term.
- tayammum-06/c5: "Whatever breaks wudu breaks tayammum" shortens "ما ينقض الأصل الذي هو
  الوضوء أو الطهر" (the original it stands in for, wudu or ghusl). Kept.
Limits unchanged: one online copy per work, and a located phrase is not a scholar's reading.
Nothing removed; no item could not be verified. content/deen/ERRATA.md is untouched: the unit
has not been released, so these are pre-release corrections recorded here.
